Sources
-------
- jesther-ai/open-u60-pro (MIT): https://github.com/jesther-ai/open-u60-pro
  The current code no longer contains its agent or web UI; both were
  rewritten.
- 33333s/zwrt-datad (MIT): https://github.com/33333s/zwrt-datad
  crates/luyaz-core's device read and write layer (ubus, state, SMS, the
  HTTP API) was moved in from a fork of it; see crates/luyaz-core/PORTING.md.
- Later changes by Wei REN (core, admin web, sentinel, Rust touch UI,
  install kit, eSIM, Tailscale), snapshot 420a6d9 (2026-09-15) and later syncs.
- touch-ui/ has its own sources and notices: see touch-ui/NOTICE.

This repository starts from a cleaned snapshot of that work, not from its git
history. Removed before publishing:
- device_report.json, ubus_probe_report.json (runtime dumps of a real device)
- vendor marketing photos used by the old admin web
- mobile/ (upstream's iOS/Android companion apps: never used here; they
  remain in the upstream repository)
- scripts/topflow/, PROFILE_MANAGER_PLAN.md (private infrastructure and
  internal notes)
- .github/workflows/release.yml (binary releases are not published yet)
- docs/designs/, .impeccable.md, SCENARIO_ENGINE_PLAN.md (design reviews,
  work-in-progress plans and internal notes)
Maintainer-specific addresses and host names were replaced with device defaults.

Third-party components
----------------------
- docs/images/ are screenshots rendered from made-up test data (mock core
  and the touch UI's offscreen render test), not from a real device.
- Rust crates: see Cargo.lock; each crate keeps its own license.
- crates/luyaz-web/static/datastar-1.0.4.js: Datastar v1.0.4
  (https://github.com/starfederation/datastar), MIT License, full text below.
- crates/luyaz-web/package.json, package-lock.json: development-only npm tools
  (browser checks, icon and contrast generators); not part of the device build.
  Each package keeps its own license.
- Prebuilt binaries used by onboard/build-kit.sh (dropbear, lpac and its Alpine
  libraries) are NOT included in this repository.

